<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tenali</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tenali is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guntur">Guntur</a> district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andhra-pradesh">Andhra Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a> delta, criss-crossed by irrigation canals. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> the nearby village of Chandavolu was a seat of the Velanati Chodas. The town is traditionally associated with Tenali Ramakrishna, the witty poet of the Vijayanagara court, and has been a notable centre of Telugu <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a>, film and literature.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tenali.jpg" alt="Tenali" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vin09 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Martyrs%27_Memorial,_Tenali.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
